Source: gnulte
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: poseidonsmile2000 <poseidonsmile2000@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/notmicrosoft2000-cmd/gnulte
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/notmicrosoft2000-cmd/gnulte.git

Package: gnulte
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4), dsniff, iproute2, procps, iputils-ping, arp-scan
Recommends: nmap
Description: GNU LAN Network Testing Environment
 Interactively simulate network degradation (latency, jitter, packet
 loss, duplication, reordering, bandwidth throttling) against devices
 on a network you own or are authorised to test.
 .
 Features: ARP-based target discovery, single/range/whitelist targeting,
 preset profiles, live multi-target dashboard, sanity validation of
 parameters, CSV export, and post-test HTML/text reports with graphs.
 .
 Authorised use only. Unauthorised network interference is illegal.